   "heading": "GEOMETRY OF HIGHER HELICITIES 1. Introduction The helicity of a vector ﬁeld in a three-dimensional space can be thought of as a real-valued version of the integral-valued Hopf invariant for a continuous map S 3 → S 2 . The latter has two well-known deﬁnitions: topological or analytic ones. Topologic",
